# Vercel CLI upload rules for a deploy run FROM THIS DIRECTORY.
#
# Since 2026/09/08 that is the fallback path only. The deploy command is
# `vercel --prod` from the REPOSITORY ROOT, which builds remotely and obeys the
# root `.vercelignore`; this file has no part in it. Do not run a plain
# (non-prebuilt) `vercel` from here — the project's Root Directory is
# `examples/passport-demo`, so an upload rooted here would have Vercel look for
# that path inside it and find nothing.
#
# Deployments from here are PREBUILT (`vercel deploy --prebuilt`), so the only
# tree the CLI ever uploads is `.vercel/output`. This file still has to exist:
# with no
# .vercelignore the CLI falls back to .gitignore, and .gitignore excludes
# precisely the trees the deployed demo must serve — `public/zk/**` (Compact
# proving keys) and `dist/` — because they are built locally and cannot be
# reproduced on a Vercel builder. Its presence takes .gitignore out of the
# decision entirely.
#
# The entries below only bite if someone runs a non-prebuilt `vercel deploy`.

node_modules
.env
.env.local
